T4b the level residual IS the running integral of the growth error -- its drift
    across the pre-seam era needs no extrapolation and no bandwidth:
      1850-1879  -0.32 +- 0.81 ppm (n=24, n_eff=5.2 at a 5.75-yr air-age width)
      1929-1958  -1.51 +- 0.66 ppm (n=70, n_eff=5.2)
      DRIFT -1.19 +- 1.04 ppm = 1.14 sigma  =>  GCB growth is LOW by 2.5 GtC
      which would inflate the pre-seam cumulative imbalance by +6 % of 44.7 GtC.
      This is SMALL and it is the only growth-side number in this file that is
      identified rather than extrapolated. It does NOT rescue the century-drift read.

    READ THIS AS A CIRCULARITY TEST, NOT A CONFIRMATION. GCB's pre-seam growth is
    Joos & Spahni 2008, itself a reconstruction of this same ice/firn record. Close
    agreement means the two are ONE object, so a model already fitted to our ice term
    is already fitted to GCB's growth, and the imbalance can only be a statement
    about EMISSIONS and SINKS.

